  "articleBody": "When you're trying to make your home safer, it's easy to make a few common missteps that can actually leave hazards in place or even create new ones. One frequent mistake is simply leaving cords draped across walkways. It might seem like a quick fix to just move it slightly, but really, you need to get them completely out of the path of travel. Another big one is ignoring those curled mat or carpet edges; they seem minor, but they're prime tripping spots. Failing to properly stretch or repair loose carpeting is also a common oversight, often because people think a small bump isn't a big deal. However, inspection checklists frequently flag abrupt edges and floor changes as major concerns, so don't assume small level changes are harmless. These kinds of hazards, especially in high-traffic areas, really need proper attention. To avoid these issues, always opt for permanent solutions over temporary fixes like tape, which can actually degrade and become a hazard itself. If you're not sure how to fix a recurring or significant issue, or if it involves modifying your flooring, it’s definitely a good idea to reach out to a professional to make sure the job gets done right and safely.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
